in this next song with me.

00:33:40.140 --> 00:33:43.170
And by that, I mean
everybody raise your hand.

00:33:43.170 --> 00:33:44.697
This is a song called "Savior."

00:33:44.697 --> 00:33:46.030
It's the last tune of the night.

00:33:46.030 --> 00:33:47.405
Thank you so, so
much for coming.

00:33:47.405 --> 00:33:48.990
This must be what
Quincy Jones felt

00:33:48.990 --> 00:33:52.260
when he first encountered Stevie
Wonder or Michael Jackson--

00:33:52.260 --> 00:33:55.500
that here's someone
who has really, really

00:33:55.500 --> 00:33:57.150
deep musical resources.

00:33:57.150 --> 00:33:59.110
He's marshalling
this at a young age,

00:33:59.110 --> 00:34:01.260
and he has phenomenal
performance skills,

00:34:01.260 --> 00:34:03.650
arranging skills,
composition skills.

00:34:03.650 --> 00:34:06.700
It's just incredible that all
this exists in a single person.

00:34:06.700 --> 00:34:08.158
Don't wanna be a--

00:34:08.158 --> 00:34:17.878
[SCATTING] I don't
